## Risks and Mitigations (Page 11)

This matrix analyzes threats to the testing process and assigns proactive countermeasures.

| Risk Description | Potential Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation Strategy | Contingency Plan |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Requirement Volatility (Scope Creep)** | High | Medium | Implement strict Change Control Board (CCB) for all requirement changes. Freeze scope after a formal sign-off. | Re-scope testing activities to focus only on approved features. |
| **Performance Bottleneck** | High | Medium | Integrate performance testing early in the cycle. Test components independently before full integration. Monitor resource usage live. | Throttle functionality or reduce concurrent user load until optimization is complete. |
| **Defect Prioritization Conflict** | Medium | High | Establish a clear, agreed-upon Severity/Priority matrix with all stakeholders. Define thresholds for P1/P2 resolution. | Escalate conflicts to the Steering Committee for immediate decision-making. |
| **Test Data Corruption** | Medium | Low | Use automated data validation scripts. Sanitize test data sets before execution. Implement secure storage protocols. | Roll back to the last clean backup; re-create data sets manually. |

